    ]
  },
  "reflection": {
    "what_people_were_focused_on": "People followed software rivalries, new internet businesses, the coming year 2000, troubles in other countries, storms, sports, and entertainment.",
    "what_actually_mattered": "The stock market fell, and the economy moved into and then out of a recession. Choosing one company instead of a basket of many companies could lead to very different results.",
    "what_faded_away": "Many people worried that computers would fail when calendars changed to 2000. After years of preparation, the new year came with little disruption. Product stories and sports soon made way for other news.",
    "what_nobody_knew": "In September 1999, no one knew when technology stocks would fall, how long the slide would last, or when the economy would go into recession. No one could know the September 11 attacks were coming. Popular companies did not make the future certain.",
